# Canvas digital twin (HTML)

Whenever you create or update a Cursor canvas (`.canvas.tsx`):

1. Also create or update a twin standalone HTML file that mirrors the report content.
2. Twin path: `reports/<same-kebab-name>.html` unless the project specifies another location (same basename as the canvas, `.html` instead of `.canvas.tsx`).
3. The HTML must be self-contained (inline CSS/JS as needed) and openable in a browser without the canvas runtime.
4. Do this in the same turn as the canvas write/update — do not wait to be asked.
5. Do not put the twin HTML inside the managed `canvases/` directory (canvas files must stay alone there).

Skip this entirely if another always-apply rule in this project disables canvas twin HTML.
